  "description": "Set up PostHog in a user's GitHub repository from a chat, without a terminal. Wizard, PostHog's setup agent, runs in the cloud, adds the SDK and first events, and opens a pull request. Use only when you can't read or edit the user's code, which is common in web chat apps such as ChatGPT on the web or Claude on the web. Typical requests: install, add, or set up PostHog in their app or repository, or open a pull request that adds PostHog. When you're working in the user's repository, use installing-posthog-in-a-codebase instead. Covers connecting GitHub, picking the repository, starting the run, polling it, and sharing the pull request.",
